# Line-ending normalization, added 2026-08-08.
#
# WHY: without this, a two-line change produced a WHOLE-FILE diff. audit-spec-contradictions.ps1 showed 709
# changed lines for a 2-line edit; `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` reduced it to 9. core.autocrlf is true, but
# with no .gitattributes the repo had a mixed CR state, so any tool writing CRLF into an LF-stored file
# rewrote every line as far as git was concerned. A diff nobody can read is a review nobody performs, and
# this estate reviews by reading diffs.
#
# `text=auto` normalizes to LF IN THE REPOSITORY while letting core.autocrlf decide the working copy, so
# nothing about how these files appear on Brad's Windows box changes.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT RENORMALIZED IN BULK. `git add --renormalize .` would fix the whole history-facing state
# in one commit touching hundreds of files - and would collide with the daily pipeline bot, which commits and
# rebases onto main on its own schedule. Files normalize as they are touched instead. The big diff never
# needs to happen; it just stops getting worse.
# eol=lf ADDED 2026-09-06 (backlog E19, ruled by Brad). `text=auto` alone normalises the
# REPOSITORY to LF and leaves core.autocrlf to decide the working copy - which on this box is
# true, so every fresh worktree and clone got CRLF while the main checkout sat at LF. Two gates
# compared bytes and went red in every new checkout over line endings rather than drift:
# grocery\audit-ghost-drift.ps1 and meal-prep\engine\golden-test.ps1.
#
# MEASURED BEFORE CHOOSING THIS. `git add --renormalize` over the whole tree changed ZERO
# files - the repository already stores LF throughout - so there was nothing to renormalise
# and the tree-side fix had to be about what a CHECKOUT writes, not about what is stored.
#
# eol=lf makes that uniform on every platform and every clone. The cost, paid once here: the
# golden fixture inputs were CRLF ON DISK in the main checkout (densities.json was 20,188
# bytes with 429 CRs against a 19,759-byte stored blob) and MANIFEST.json had recorded their
# hashes from those CRLF bytes. Forcing LF invalidated all 23. They are re-recorded in the
# same commit - line endings only, no input regenerated, no expected output moved.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.wav  binary
*.zip  binary
*.db   binary
*.sqlite binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
